programmeDeliveryTrackRecord:
PROGRAM DELIVERY TRACK RECORD
The Rev. Fr. Moses Orshio Adasu University Innovation Hub, in collaboration with relevant University units, including the Consultancy Services and Directorate of ICT, has experience in the design and delivery of digital literacy, e-learning, ICT, entrepreneurship, and professional capacity-building programmes.
1. Mandatory University E-Learning Proficiency Course
The University delivers a mandatory 5-day E-Learning Proficiency Course for newly admitted undergraduate students.
Target Audience: Newly admitted undergraduate students.
Objective: To equip new students with essential digital literacy skills, introduce them to the University's ICT and e-learning platforms, and prepare them for hybrid and blended learning.
Delivery: Practical, hands-on training and orientation.
 The programme included the E-Learning training for new students, with Batch A commencing on 10 November 2025.
2. Public, Community and Graduate ICT Training
The Consultancy Services unit has also provided public-facing professional ICT training designed to improve employability and digital skills among secondary school graduates, job seekers, young people, and career changers.
Key areas include:
Basic Computer Skills and Internet Literacy;
Typing and Office Productivity;
Web Development — HTML, CSS, JavaScript and PHP;
Data Analytics and Statistical Computing, including SPSS and MySQL;
Introduction to Artificial Intelligence and emerging technologies.
3. Professional Certification and Corporate Training
The Consultancy Services, in collaboration with the Directorate of ICT and other relevant University units, supports technical and professional training programmes, including:
Cisco CCNA certification preparation;
CompTIA A+ certification preparation;
Oracle SQL training;
Digital literacy and productivity training;
ICT infrastructure and technology management;
Customized ICT capacity-building programmes for government, educational institutions and other organizations.
4. Community and Institutional Capacity Building
The University has also participated in digital-skills and ICT capacity-building initiatives targeted at teachers, students, graduates, public-sector personnel and members of the wider community. These programmes are designed to promote digital inclusion, employability, technology adoption, innovation and lifelong learning.
